      "text": "Every glib, arrogant, virtue-signalling celebrity who’s broadcast the lie that  kids will kill themselves if not allowed to transition deserves to have this read aloud to them non-stop through a megaphone for a year.",
      "quote": {
        "author": "k_mahlburg",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1877172257300299776/GcJrYdGN_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-09-19 18:45:02",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-09-19T10:45:02.000Z",
        "id": "2101261275472760944",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSkt-v2bkAEjTNe.jpg?name=small"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "height": 990,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSkt-v2bkAEjTNe.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1486
          }
        ],
        "name": "Kurt Mahlburg",
        "text": "A landmark Finnish study has found a sharp rise in psychiatric illness among adolescents following sex-alteration procedures.\n\nThe peer-reviewed study, published in Acta Paediatrica, tracked every young person under 23 who contacted Finland's gender clinics between 1996 and 2019.\n\nA total 2,083 individuals were studied, with 16,643 matched controls. They were followed for up to 25 years.\n\nFinland's health registers are mandatory, which means no one opts out — this is the complete national picture.\n\nThe numbers: psychiatric morbidity rose from 9.8% to 60.7% in adolescents who underwent feminising reassignment, and from 21.6% to 54.5% in masculinising reassignment.\n\nEven after adjusting for prior psychiatric history, gender-referred adolescents faced five times the risk of male population controls, and three times the risk of female controls.\n\n\"Psychiatric needs do not subside after medical gender reassignment,\" the authors concluded.\n\nReferrals after 2010 arrived sicker. 47.9% had already needed psychiatric treatment before their first clinic visit, against 15.3% among controls.\n\nThe authors' read: for some adolescents, gender distress may be secondary to other mental health challenges.\n\nThe evidence keeps mounting. The silencing continues anyway.\n\nHow many more adolescents will be told this is \"care\"?",
        "url": "https://x.com/k_mahlburg/status/2101261275472760944",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": {
